4TH ASCENSION GAME SUMMARY ("I Wish I May, I Wish I Might")

Raynes the Student of Fire  St:18/24 Dx:18 Co:18 In:16 Wi:18 Ch:18  Neutral
Astral Plane $:0  HP:216(270) Pw:23(209) AC:-35 Xp:27/70921814 T:60148

This is the first time I ascended a Monk; I like it. Also my first PYEC
(though I'm blasted when using it), first round Medusa island, first time
using purple worms as pets.

I was trying for wieldless and vegetarian, and I didn't get either one: I
keep making pick-axe errors, and I had to eat a lizard. Lessons learned
for next time. As an additional roleplaying affectation, I decided not to
use iron armor or weapons at any time (this one I was able to achieve).

I decided to take on the Castle without MR (to get it from the /oW) and I
quickly learned from a lich that I've been taking MR for granted playing
Wizard. :-) Of course he crumbled my best piece of armor and the [oWW I
rode in on. I found a lot of blind spots like this in my playing.

Given the dire warnings about Kaen I put him off until I was halfway
through Gehennom, and ultimately I think I over-prepared.

I got an insane number of wishes (15); two wands of wishing, three throne
wishes (plus two throne genocides), and three magic lamps. Needless to say
I had no problem with my ascension kit. Finally had a game where I had a
T-shirt and the means to enchant it (nice that it was a Monk game).

I stumbled on the portal to Astral before I was ready, after using too
much Pw on Water. I didn't have =oConflict, and nearly died; in retrospect
I clearly wasn't well prepared. =oRegeneration and my very low AC made it
possible to squeak through, with a lucky first guess as to the altar.

[Screen shot and final stats are at the bottom, after the game timeline
and "lessons learned" (my running notes during the game)]


